<title>USA: Ault Inc Q2 Dec 1 net, sales higher.</title>
<headline>Ault Inc Q2 Dec 1 net, sales higher.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			$  0.12		   $ 0.09</p>
<p> Net			    290			200</p>
<p> Revs			 9,248		    7,711</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,405		    2,193</p>
<p>	  SIX MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			$  0.22		  $  0.12</p>
<p> Net			    517			262</p>
<p> Revs			17,926		   14,592</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,396		    2,176</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Ault said it has used substantially all of its net operating loss carryforwards from prior years, although it continues to offset a portion of its taxable income with certain applicable tax credits. As a result, its effective income tax rate was about 24 percent for the second quarter and first half of fiscal 1997. Substantially no income tax expense was incurred in the same periods of fiscal 1996.</p>
<p>	  ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
